<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Istiqlal Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Independence Party (Morocco)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Istiqlal ('Independence') Party is a Moroccan nationalist party founded in 1944, when it issued a manifesto demanding independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Led by Allal al-Fassi and Ahmed Balafrej, it worked with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-v-of-adal">Sultan Muhammad V</a> and led the struggle that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1956. It remains one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>'s main conservative parties.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/istiqlal-party.jpg" alt="Istiqlal Party" width="294" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Parti de l'Istiqlalحزب الإستقلال · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_-_Parti_de_l%27Istiqlal.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
